SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "SBRC.sbrc_rr_buildings_road", "instrument_version": "SBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2017@2024-10-28", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Table 6.2.14 AO1.3(a)", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": 10, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2024-10-28", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "SOUTH_BURNETT"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "SBRC:RURAL_RESIDENTIAL"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "sbrc_rr_buildings_road", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"min_road_setback\", \"operator\": \">=\", \"value\": 10, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": null}\nStructure scope 'buildings' mapped by keyword to ['ANY'] (default)\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO - s1.6(4) says the building assessment provisions in the scheme are those in Table 1.6.1, which lists only the bushfire prone area designation; zone-code setbacks are not declared as QDC alternative provisions (s33 Building Act)\nResearcher notes: PO1 refers to \"Buildings and structures\". Table 5.5.14: a dwelling house is accepted development unless it includes a secondary dwelling, which makes it ADSR against Section 4 only (no setbacks). Code assessment applies \"If not accepted development subject to requirements\", and s5.3.3(4)(b) may limit that to the failed Section 4 matters. So whether AO1.3 reaches a dwelling house or its outbuildings needs curator review."}$q$::jsonb);
