SELECT define_rule($q${"rule_id": "SBRC.sbrc_township_buildings_road", "instrument_version": "SBRC_PLANNING_SCHEME_2017@2024-10-28", "topic": "SETBACK.FRONTAGE", "title": "Table 6.2.16 AO2.2 and AO2.3", "role": "REQUIREMENT", "regime": "PLANNING", "enforceability": "DEEMED_TO_COMPLY", "provision_kind": "ACCEPTABLE_OUTCOME", "measurement": "SCHEME_SETBACK_FRONT", "operator": ">=", "value": {"op": "unencoded", "text": "if adjoining buildings exist and avg(adjoining setbacks) <= 6 then setback = avg(2 adjoining) else setback >= 3", "extracted_value": null, "extracted_operator": "conditional"}, "unit": "m", "on_noncompliance": "PLANNING_APPROVAL_REQUIRED", "effective_from": "2024-10-28", "verification": "VERIFIED_VERBATIM", "automatable": false, "scopes": [{"level": "LOCAL_GOVERNMENT", "lg": "SOUTH_BURNETT"}, {"level": "ZONE", "zone": "SBRC:TOWNSHIP"}], "subjects": ["ANY"], "sources": [{"key": "sbrc_township_buildings_road", "role": "PRIMARY"}], "interpretation_notes": "AUTO-IMPORTED (draft). Extracted structure: {\"parameter\": \"road_alignment_setback\", \"operator\": \"conditional\", \"value\": null, \"unit\": \"m\", \"conditions\": [\"adjoining buildings on both sides with average setback <= 6 m: equal to the average setback of the 2 adjoining buildings\", \"no adjoining buildings, or average adjoining setback > 6 m: >= 3 m\"], \"exceptions\": [], \"formula_text\": \"if adjoining buildings exist and avg(adjoining setbacks) <= 6 then setback = avg(2 adjoining) else setback >= 3\"}\nStructure scope 'buildings' mapped by keyword to ['ANY'] (default)\nAlternative provision to QDC/QHC: NO - s1.6(4) says the building assessment provisions in the scheme are those in Table 1.6.1, which lists only the bushfire prone area designation; zone-code setbacks are not declared as QDC alternative provisions (s33 Building Act)\nResearcher notes: Table 5.5.16: a dwelling house is accepted development if it does not involve a secondary dwelling. With a secondary dwelling it is ADSR against \"Sections 1, 2, 3 & 7\", so AO2.2/AO2.3 apply. AO2.2 sets an equal (averaging) setback rather than a minimum. It applies to every road alignment."}$q$::jsonb);
